{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03532",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 4.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Hello, sorry about the delay, do sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.13,
      "end_seconds": 10.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Hello, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.27,
      "end_seconds": 13.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Have you been waiting long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.91,
      "end_seconds": 18.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Only about ten minutes, uh, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.71,
      "end_seconds": 21.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.78,
      "end_seconds": 28.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "It's a sore spot on the front of my shin, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.82,
      "end_seconds": 32.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.93,
      "end_seconds": 36.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Moderate, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.93,
      "end_seconds": 43.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "So, is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.49,
      "end_seconds": 48.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.54,
      "end_seconds": 51.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Does anything help it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.02,
      "end_seconds": 55.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I get some relief from rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.8,
      "end_seconds": 60.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "What about pain at night, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.2,
      "end_seconds": 67.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Yeah. Five days, I'd say. As for pain at night, severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.98,
      "end_seconds": 70.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Any sign of fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.69,
      "end_seconds": 74.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Definitely no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.52,
      "end_seconds": 78.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "I follow. Did you get injury, swelling or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.0,
      "end_seconds": 86.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.29,
      "end_seconds": 93.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "So, anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.02,
      "end_seconds": 97.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "No, you know, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.92,
      "end_seconds": 101.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.02,
      "end_seconds": 106.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "No, you know, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.37,
      "end_seconds": 110.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.85,
      "end_seconds": 115.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.86,
      "end_seconds": 119.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Okay, anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.07,
      "end_seconds": 124.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.7,
      "end_seconds": 131.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.4,
      "end_seconds": 136.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Alendronate. I take it once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.26,
      "end_seconds": 142.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.04,
      "end_seconds": 148.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "70 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.91,
      "end_seconds": 163.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.93,
      "end_seconds": 168.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I have thin bones, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.68,
      "end_seconds": 174.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.62,
      "end_seconds": 178.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.12,
      "end_seconds": 180.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.67,
      "end_seconds": 184.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.83,
      "end_seconds": 188.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.59,
      "end_seconds": 203.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.38,
      "end_seconds": 230.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 109 over 76, respiratory rate 14. And pulse is 76 beats a minute, temperature 36.7."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.42,
      "end_seconds": 235.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.94,
      "end_seconds": 240.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.88,
      "end_seconds": 245.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.64,
      "end_seconds": 261.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.6,
      "end_seconds": 264.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.96,
      "end_seconds": 287.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "There is a very localised tender spot on the bone and hopping on that leg hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.0,
      "end_seconds": 307.02,
      "duration_seconds": 17.02,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Having listened and examined, this looks most like a possible stress fracture rather than shin splints. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Shin splints is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.2,
      "end_seconds": 332.28,
      "duration_seconds": 12.08,
      "text": "An MRI of the shin is what I'd like next, for possible stress fracture. Let's book a vitamin D level to look into stress fracture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.93,
      "end_seconds": 337.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.04,
      "end_seconds": 353.17,
      "duration_seconds": 15.13,
      "text": "Stop running, no impact exercise until the scan, swimming or cycling is fine. Book a review after the scan. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.66,
      "end_seconds": 359.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "So, I come back after the scan. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.27,
      "end_seconds": 365.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.6,
      "end_seconds": 371.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}